{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166646 :question/id #uuid "26cd55d1-dc94-507c-bcf9-13d619493184" :question/math-academy-id "e-8454"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f97720d6-2c67-5017-bf20-8045a8bb30b5" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167436} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167519} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186538970} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186538980} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186539028}] :knowledge-point/title "Completing the Square to Compute a Hyperbolic Arcosecant Integral"} :step/id #uuid "60e05d0f-21d0-5754-8412-0060020c8e21" :step/math-academy-id 31486 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167646}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167646 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166809 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166647 :question/id #uuid "aa11660f-ce84-52df-bcc4-45a6d63b6d7e" :question/math-academy-id "e-8455"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6640d03e-5194-5a31-9315-007e59732446" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167437} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167438} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186538952} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186538982} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186539017}] :knowledge-point/title "Completing the Square to Compute a Hyperbolic Arcotangent Integral"} :step/id #uuid "754cf784-bf5d-5f7b-8c12-79b57d3e1f4b" :step/math-academy-id 31487} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167709 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186168099 :tutorial/content "We can also complete the square to integrate hyperbolic *arcsecant*, *arccosecant*, and *arccotangent*.\n\nFor example, let's consider the integral\n\n$$\n\\int \\dfrac{1}{\\left(x+3\\right)\\sqrt{-x^2-6x}} \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nAs it is, this integral doesn't resemble any of the basic integrals we have encountered so far. However, we can complete the square for the argument of the square root in the denominator, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}^{2}-6x & =-({x}^{2}+6x) \\\\  & =-({x}^{2}+2\\cdot 3x+{3}^{2}-{3}^{2}) \\\\  & =-((x+3)^{2}-9) \\\\  & =9-(x+3)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we plug the above into our integral and collect a factor of $9$ under the square root, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{(x+3)\\sqrt{-{x}^{2}-6x}}\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{(x+3)\\sqrt{9-(x+3)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{3(x+3)\\sqrt{1-{(\\frac{x+3}{3})}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\int \\frac{1}{(\\frac{x+3}{3})\\sqrt{1-{(\\frac{x+3}{3})}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis now looks more familiar! Let $u = \\dfrac {x+3}{3}.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}=\\dfrac{1}{3}\n\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\n\\textrm{d}x = 3\\,\\textrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe can now write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{(x+3)\\sqrt{-{x}^{2}-6x}}\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{9}\\int \\frac{1}{(\\frac{x+3}{3})\\sqrt{1-{(\\frac{x+3}{3})}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\int \\frac{1}{u\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot (3\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{u\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a basic integral for an inverse reciprocal hyperbolic function, and we can solve it in one step:\n$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{u\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arsech}⁡u+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(\\frac{x+3}{3})+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "5f0c7466-a41d-5101-b125-8e6f68fba3ea" :tutorial/math-academy-id 5218 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "98b81a6a-5fdd-53d9-a014-da6921adf68b" :step/math-academy-id 32703 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167644}}] :activity/title "Integration Using Inverse Reciprocal Hyperbolic Functions and Completing the Square" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186167030}]}
